#
# Base: `grok completions zsh` from the 1.0.16 binary. grok ships a static
# clap_complete generator and post-processes it itself
# (completions_cmd.rs::fix_zsh_root_prompt_positional) to work around
# clap-rs/clap#6282, where the optional root `[PROMPT]` positional makes clap
# dispatch on `$line[2]` and break `grok worktree <TAB>`. The shipped output
# already has that fixed — do not re-fix it.
#
# Items marked "(hidden)" are accepted by the CLI but suppressed from
# `--help`. Two distinct kinds, because clap treats them differently:
#
#   1. `hide = true` args and commands. clap_complete does *not* filter these,
#      so they were already completable but unlabelled; here they are labelled.
#      Found by diffing the generated script against every `--help` in the
#      tree, then confirming each against the 1.0.16 binary.
#        * root flags:  --background-wait-timeout --client-identifier
#                       --compaction-detail --compaction-mode
#                       --experimental-memory --force-login --fs-read
#                       --fs-write --hunk-tracker-mode --installer --leader
#                       --load --log-sampling --memory-flush --no-ask-user
#                       --no-auto-update --no-leader --no-memory
#                       --no-wait-for-background --storage-mode --terminal
#                       --todo-gate --trust
#        * commands:    share, workspace (+ its start/pause/resume/stop/
#                       restart/status subcommands, and status's `list` alias)
#        * login:       --legacy --devbox
#        * update:      --enterprise --trigger --auto
#        * mcp add:     --command --args --url --type
#
#   2. Non-visible `alias = ...` entries. clap_complete drops these outright,
#      so they were previously uncompletable; they are inserted here.
#        * --allowedTools (--allow), --disallowedTools (--deny),
#          --print (--single), --append-system-prompt (--rules),
#          --system-prompt (--system-prompt-override), --yolo and
#          --dangerously-skip-permissions (--always-approve),
#          --trust-folder (--trust), login --oidc (--oauth),
#          worktree prune (gc)
#
# Scope is not uniform, and the binary enforces it. `--leader` / `--no-leader`
# are hidden at the root but documented on `grok agent`; `--no-auto-update`
# likewise on `grok agent leader`; `--memory-flush` exists only at the root.
# The root `--always-approve` carries both `yolo` and
# `dangerously-skip-permissions`, but the `grok agent` copy carries only
# `yolo` — `grok agent --dangerously-skip-permissions` is rejected.
#
# NOT a typo: `grok agent ----reauthenticate` really does take four hyphens.
# The source writes `visible_alias = "--reauthenticate"` with the dashes
# inside the alias name, so clap registers it as `--reauthenticate` and the
# spelling on the command line grows two more. The binary rejects the
# two-hyphen form.
#
# Visible aliases (`v`, `disk-usage`, `worktree ls`, `plugin rm`/`remove`,
# `workspace list`, `--effort`, `--ref`, `login --device-code`) are documented
# by clap in a trailing "[aliases: ...]" note and emitted by the generator, so
# they are completable without being hidden. Reading only the leading token of
# each help line mistakes every one of them for a hidden item.
#
# Cross-checked against xai-org/grok-build at commit bb7f39d5 (crate
# xai-grok-pager 1.0.13). The public mirror lags the release, so every item
# was confirmed against the installed 1.0.16 binary with
# `grok [SUBCMD] <FLAG>=ZZ --zzz-sentinel-flag` (undefined iff clap answers
# "unexpected argument '<FLAG>'") and `grok help <PATH>` for commands.
# `login --devbox` is one such case: the mirror has it behind `#[arg(skip)]`
# for the `devbox-login` feature, and the shipped binary accepts it.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


